content.text:
Build clean.

## What was wrong, briefly

**The frontend code:**
- Initial fetch was sorted (`.order("timestamp", ascending: true)`) ✓
- But Realtime INSERT subscription just appended new rows: `setMessages(p => [...p, payload.new])` ✗

**Why timestamps come out of order:**
- PersonaPlex flushes `agent_text_buf` on phrase boundaries → slight delay
- Scribe transcripts stream more eagerly → less delay
- A caller "Hi" at +0:16 can arrive in Supabase / via Realtime AFTER an agent fragment timestamped +0:18 finally flushes
- Once it lands, it gets appended to the END of the messages array even though it belongs earlier

**The fix:** sort the messages array by `timestamp ASC, id ASC` (id is `bigserial` so it tie-breaks on DB insertion order) right before passing to `groupTranscriptBubbles`. Memoized so it only re-sorts when `messages` changes.

```typescript
const sortedMessages = useMemo(() => {
  return [...messages].sort((a, b) => {
    const ta = Date.parse(a.timestamp);
    const tb = Date.parse(b.timestamp);
    if (ta !== tb) return ta - tb;
    return a.id - b.id;
  });
}, [messages]);
```

This is **frontend-only** — backend timestamps are correct, the database is correct, the issue was purely in render-order.

## Side benefit

The cross-role lookback grouping (Sarah's continuous utterance bridging caller interruptions) now also works correctly on out-of-order Realtime streams, since the input is properly chronological before grouping runs.

Want me to commit + push this fix?

